  "mechanism_evidence": {
    "verify_step_law": "verify-step GPU time = 17.0-17.3 ms + 176-179 us x (expert misses on the slower EP rank, summed over the 48 MoE layers), R^2 >= 0.997, hot 64-96, measured with CUDA events in research sessions",
    "policy_effect_heldout": "same VRAM (76 slots/layer/GPU), held-out prompts, two LRU sessions vs LRFU / per-layer / both: max-rank misses -6.6% / -7.5% / -14.2%, verify step -2.9% / -4.2% / -7.1%; an offline replay of the LRU session's routing predicted each change within ~2 points",
    "combined_same_day": "256K profile vs two F5 sessions: misses -12 to -13%, verify step -6%; 128K profile: misses -37 to -40%, verify step -19 to -20%; worst-8K-chunk driver-free memory 321-335 MiB (256K) and 281-295 MiB (128K) versus 193-207 MiB for F5",
    "kernel_check": "the runtime LRU kernel replayed 44,502 recorded calls: 100.000% of per-call miss counts equal to a reference LRU model with the policies off; 99.95-99.99% with LRFU (ties and float32 keys), including forced key rebasing",
    "prefill_trims": "reference drops in the PLE forward and the decoder loop: transient per 8K chunk 1,126 -> 868 MiB; greedy tokens identical in 12 comparisons; logprob differences equal to the control's own run-to-run variation (median 0.0076 vs 0.0051 nats, p95 0.77 vs 0.81)"
  },
  "rejected": [
    "hot80 at 256K (trims, uniform): passed 262,016+128 once with ~100 MiB driver-free, then with the policies ran out of memory on a 320 MiB request with 786 MiB reserved but unallocated (allocator fragmentation)",
    "hot96 at 128K with the policies: out of memory on the same 320 MiB request (MTP draft prefill), 3 MiB driver-free at the first 8K chunk; hot100 at 128K ran out of memory even without the policies"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "One session per configuration; per-request decode varies by about +-10% with MTP acceptance, so compare the reciprocal-mean rates, not single requests.",
    "Per-layer sizes add 50-170 MiB of non-PyTorch GPU memory (one Humming configuration and kernel set per distinct slot count) and first-start compiles: about 8 minutes of LRU-kernel compilation on an empty JIT cache, 4.8-5.7 s TTFT on the first short request of a session (F5: 1.9 s).",
    "The first 262,016+128 request of every session, including F5, includes first-use compiles (decode p99 chunk gap 229-256 ms)."
  ]
